{:now [{:claim "Retrograde motion is relative motion"
        :modern "The direction of a planet seen from the Earth is the angle of the difference of two position vectors; its rate turns negative near the closest approach exactly when the inner body has the larger linear speed."
        :tex "\\dot\\lambda=\\frac{G_x\\dot G_y-G_y\\dot G_x}{|G|^2},\\qquad G=P-E"}
       {:claim "Changing the frame does not change the sky"
        :modern "Ptolemy's epicycle and Copernicus' orbit are the same vector sum G = P + (-E) read in two frames: a change of origin, a Galilean symmetry of the kinematics. What the heliocentric frame adds is that the scale of every planet is fixed in units of the Earth's orbit."
        :tex "G = P + (-E) = C + (u,v)"}
       {:claim "Synodic and sidereal periods are beat frequencies"
        :modern "Two uniform rotations of frequencies 1/E and 1/P meet with the difference frequency, as two tones beat; the same relation fixes conjunctions of satellites and the lunar month."
        :tex "\\frac1S=\\left|\\frac1E-\\frac1P\\right|"}]
 :fields [{:field :mechanics-physics :label "Astronomy" :how "The heliocentric order fixed the relative distances of the planets for the first time, from the epicycle ratios alone." :example "Mars at 1.52 Earth radii from Ptolemy's 39;30 epicycle; Jupiter at 5.2 from 11;30."}
          {:field :mechanics-physics :label "Physics" :how "Choosing the frame in which motion is simplest is the first step of mechanics; Copernicus' frame is the one in which Kepler and Newton could see the laws." :example "Retrograde loops disappear in the Sun's frame and appear in the Earth's."}
          {:field :mechanics-physics :label "Engineering" :how "Synodic periods set launch windows: a spacecraft to Mars leaves once per Earth-Mars synodic period." :example "About every 780 days, Copernicus' 779 days 56 minutes."}
          {:field :logic-computing :label "Computing" :how "Integrating coupled rotations step by step is how ephemerides are computed today." :example "The RK4 integration of the moving Earth and Mars in this notebook."}]
 :tangents [{:series :physics :hook "From Copernicus' circles to Kepler's ellipses and Newton's inverse square: the frame that made the laws visible."}]
